==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|encombrer|lang=fro}}, from {{term|en-}} + {{term|combrer||to hinder}}; see {{term|cumber}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} to [[load]] down something with a [[burden]]
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} to [[restrict]] or [[block]] something with a [[hindrance]] or [[impediment]]
#* {{quote-book
|year=1906 – 1921
|author=[[w:John Galsworthy|John Galsworthy]]
|title=[[w:The Forsyte Saga|The Forsyte Saga]]
|volume=1
|chapter=Encounter
|passage=He [Timothy Forsyte] had never committed the imprudence of marrying or encumbering himself in any way with children.}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} to add a [[legal]] [[claim]] or other [[obligation]]

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:hinder]]

====Antonyms====
* [[disencumber]], [[unload]], [[unencumber]]

====Derived terms====
* [[encumbrance]]
* [[encumbrous]]

